WEBVTT

00:25:28.663 --> 00:25:31.288
And then I might also be interested
in whether they you know,

00:25:31.288 --> 00:25:33.079
they're aligned on our organizational
values.

00:25:33.579 --> 00:25:34.871
And then once I've done that,

00:25:35.079 --> 00:25:37.788
I want to form an overall impression
of the candidate,

00:25:37.788 --> 00:25:41.538
because I may have picked up on other
pieces of information that didn't fit

00:25:41.538 --> 00:25:42.538
the model that I had.

00:25:43.246 --> 00:25:44.496
I think that's about right.

00:25:44.871 --> 00:25:48.746
It's such a powerful step that
I think should bring

00:25:48.746 --> 00:25:51.954
the best of both worlds from algorithms
and human judgment.

00:25:52.746 --> 00:25:55.246
There's something that's a little
puzzling to me about it, though,

00:25:55.246 --> 00:26:00.163
which is why are managers and people in
general so enamored with intuition?